tivity, could also contribute to the observed decrease. In conclusion, while the inference that the Archive is processing and preserving evidence supports the observed decrease in markers, a missing control would be evidence of markers before any public-search capabilities were used. If the markers naturally decrease without any resident activity, it would challenge the inference.",
